  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "In a July 22, 2026 USDA press release, Scott Hutchins said USDA is taking concrete steps to give scientists modern tools and that partners using AI tools could unlock faster discoveries with germplasm data and help grow better crops. He also said AI would help sort through germplasm, sequencing, and catalogs and that incorporating AI and analytical advances could improve efficiency. Hutchins referred to using artificial intelligence with remote sensing and automation and described AI as a check for anomalies not identified in the normal process.",
   "sids": [
    "s1",
    "s2",
    "s3",
    "s4",
    "s5"
   ],
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "In a July 22, 2026 USDA press release, Scott Hutchins said USDA is taking concrete steps to give scientists modern tools and that partners using AI tools could unlock faster discoveries with germplasm data and help grow better crops.",
